    "example.table.more": "Load 4 more",
    "example.table.more-status": "{count} more rows. {total} altogether.",
    "example.table.note-invoices": "`note` adds the line under the caption, and a cell can hold a component such as a `Tag`.",
    "example.table.note-status": "`low` and `high` band the values, and `tone_below`, `tone_within` and `tone_above` colour them. A cell's own `tone` wins.",
    "example.table.note-totals": "Search for a client to see the total follow. `aggregate` counts again from the rows still showing.",
    "example.table.note-groups": "`collapsible` folds a section. Each group ends with a row counting its own rows, and several can be open at once.",
    "example.table.note-usage": "A `Meter`, a `Progress` and an `Info` all sit inside cells. The second import bar has no value, so it is indeterminate.",
    "example.table.note-team": "Choosing rows: a real checkbox with a real name and value, so the choice submits with no script at all. Shift and a click extends from the last row touched, the box in the heading has the third state — some, not all — and a `disabled` row is still read, still copied and still counted.",
    "example.table.note-export": "**Export takes what is showing**: the visible columns, the rows a search left, and any chosen rows.",
    "example.table.note-search": "What is typed hides the rows matching no searched column, rather than removing them from the markup.",
    "example.table.note-deploys": "`pinned` holds a column in place while the rest scroll. `tone` takes any name the colour system declares, not one of a fixed list.",
    "example.table.note-more": "`more_src` fetches the next rows. The button is always in the markup, and the script presses it when it scrolls into view.",
    "example.table.note-density": "`density` sets the row height. `zebra` counts only the rows on screen, so the stripes stay even when a search hides one.",
    "example.table.note-sticky": "`sticky_header` needs a `height` as well. Scroll the box and the column names stay in place.",
    "example.table.note-stack": "`layout: TableLayout::Stack` turns each row into label-and-value pairs. `auto` is the same layout, measured on the box.",
    "example.table.note-columns": "Drag a column's edge to resize it, or reach the handle with the keyboard and press Alt with the arrow keys.",
    "example.table.note-empty": "Search for something that is not here to see the empty row.",
    "example.table.note-column-width": "`width` sizes a column through a real `<colgroup>`, which the browser lays out with no script.",
    "example.table.note-column-sort": "`sort_as` declares how a column sorts. Guessing is how `10` comes to sort before `9`.",
    "example.table.note-column-hide": "`hidden` starts a column hidden in the markup, so the first paint is already right. `hideable` puts it in the columns menu.",
    "example.table.note-section-head": "`<thead>` is what puts the column names into every announcement a screen reader makes.",
    "example.table.note-section-foot": "A `<tfoot>` stays at the bottom however the body is sorted, and only its cells may carry an `aggregate`.",
    "example.table.note-section-group": "A collapsible group: `label` draws a heading row that spans the table, and the script turns it into a real button with a real `aria-expanded`. Rendered **open**, because a fold that cannot be undone is a group that has disappeared.",
    "example.table.note-section-none": "With no head at all, each row's own heading is its name, marked with `scope=\"row\"`.",
    "example.table.note-row-tone": "`tone` washes a row and draws a rule down its leading edge. The `Tag` in the row carries the same state in words.",
    "example.table.note-row-expand": "`expandable` opens a detail row of its own, so it moves with sorting and it prints.",
    "example.table.note-row-select": "A shared `select_name` makes the radios one answer with several values. A disabled row is still read and counted.",
    "example.table.note-row-emphasis": "`subtle` closes a section and `strong` is the row that answers the whole table.",
    "example.table.note-cell-numeric": "`align: TableCellAlign::Numeric` also turns on tabular figures, so digits line up under digits. `sort_value` is what the cell sorts by.",
    "example.table.note-cell-wrap": "`Truncate` clips with an ellipsis and keeps the whole value in the markup, so it is still read and copied. `Nowrap` keeps one line.",
    "example.table.note-cell-span": "Where a span moves a cell, `column` says which column it is still in, so the totals stay on the right one.",
    "example.table.note-cell-label": "Narrow the frame to see the labels appear. Each is `aria-hidden`, since the column heading already names the value.",
    "example.table.note-cell-aggregate": "`aggregate: TableCellAggregate::Sum` totals the rows that are showing, and totals again when a search hides one.",
    "example.table.note-header-scope": "`scope=\"row\"` makes a screen reader name the row before reading a value.",
    "example.table.note-header-sort": "`column` ties the heading to the declaration that made it sortable, so a spanning heading sorts the right column.",
    "example.table.note-header-align": "`align: TableHeaderCellAlign::Numeric` puts the heading over its own digits. The second column shows what happens without it.",
    "example.table.note-header-group": "A heading spanning a run of columns needs `scope: \"colgroup\"`, so the span means something to a screen reader too.",
    "example.table.note-sort": "Sorting has three states, and the third is the order the table arrived in. A two-state control loses that order on the first press.",
    "example.overview.disclosure.a11y": "The element is the browser's own, so the role, the state and the keyboard arrive with it — and nothing here moves the focus, because this is not a dialog.",
    "example.overview.list.declare": "Declare the component in the specification, with a sentence for every prop.",
    "example.overview.list.build": "Run the build, which writes both implementations and this page from it.",
    "example.overview.list.examples": "Write the examples, because a component nobody has shown how to use fails the check.",
    "example.overview.badge.reviews": "Reviews",
    "example.overview.badge.waiting": "128 reviews waiting for you",
    "example.overview.error-summary.note": "A form the server rejected: the messages at the top, each a real `<a href>` to its control. `focus` is off on this page of examples.",
    "example.overview.list-item.corners": "How round every corner in the page is, from square to circular.",
    "example.overview.paragraph.lead": "Every colour in this system is asked for by name. A component says `danger`, and the palette answers with whatever `danger` means in the appearance the reader is in.",
    "example.overview.paragraph.body": "That is what lets one word be right twice. Nothing carries a hex code, nothing has to be re-checked when the palette moves, and the page in the dark appearance is the same page rather than a second copy of it kept in step by hand.",
    "example.overview.paragraph.note": "A name no family declares fails the build rather than resolving to nothing on the screen, which is the quietest way a colour disappears.",
    "example.overview.code-block.caption": "The early return is the whole point: a scope that changes nothing stamps nothing.",
