    "example.overview.prose.heading": "The measure",
    "example.overview.prose.lead": "A reading column caps its own line length, so a paragraph stays about seventy characters wide however wide the page around it is.",
    "example.overview.prose.body": "Everything inside it inherits that cap. The headings, the lists and the quotations all wrap at the same measure, so a reader finds the next line without hunting for it. Widening the window makes the page wider and the column stays where it was.",
