    "example.divider.note-named": "A rule between two blocks that have names. Between siblings of one kind, more space says it and a rule does not.",
    "example.divider.note-label": "A labelled divider is a `<div role=\"separator\">`, because an `<hr>` holds no content. The word is written again as `aria-label`.",
    "example.divider.note-vertical": "A vertical rule between two groups on one line. It takes its height from the row rather than from a number.",
    "example.divider.note-weight": "Three thicknesses, from the three border tokens. The heaviest is the one a `Field` draws down the edge of a refused answer.",
    "example.divider.note-decorative": "Out of the accessibility tree. Use it where the rule repeats a boundary the heading above it already draws.",
